  "description": "Learn the names of common animals in Chinese and how to describe them with simple sentences.",
  "guidebook": "## Animals in Chinese 🐾\n\nIn this unit, you'll learn the names of six common animals and how to make simple sentences about them.\n\n### Key Grammar: Using 是 (shì) for \"to be\"\nTo say \"It is a dog,\" use the structure:\n**Subject + 是 + Noun**\n- 这是狗。 (Zhè shì gǒu.) — This is a dog.\n\n### Using 很 (hěn) for descriptions\nTo describe an animal, use:\n**Subject + 很 + Adjective**\n- 猫很小。 (Māo hěn xiǎo.) — The cat is very small.\n\n### Measure word: 只 (zhī)\nWhen counting animals, use the measure word **只**:\n- 一只鸟 (yì zhī niǎo) — one bird\n\n### Negation with 不 (bù)\nTo make a sentence negative, place **不** before the verb or adjective:\n- 鱼不大。 (Yú bù dà.) — The fish is not big.\n\nPractice combining these patterns to build longer sentences!",
